bash-5.2$ ./build/discobox --color always --help
Discobox runs coding agents in isolated sandboxes on this machine.

Make a discobox with "discobox run":

  discobox run . 'fix the failing tests'
  discobox run -H codex -d . 'fix the failing tests'

With no command it shows this help. Open the console with "discobox console".
See "discobox run --help" for everything run takes.

[1mUsage:[0m
  discobox [command] [flags]

[1mBasic commands:[0m
  [36mrun, new, create, r, n[39m    Run a prompt in a new discobox
  [36mls, list[39m                  List discoboxes
  [36mattach[39m                    Open a discobox: its terminal and what runs beside it
  [36mexec[39m                      Run a command in a discobox, or its login shell
  [36mstart[39m                     Start discoboxes
  [36mstop[39m                      Stop discoboxes
  [36mrestart[39m                   Restart discoboxes
  [36mrm, delete, remove[39m        Archive discoboxes
  [36mrename[39m                    Name a discobox
  [36mtag[39m                       Set and remove a discobox's tags

[1mAutomation:[0m
  [36msend[39m                      Send text to a discobox's terminal
  [36msend-key[39m                  Send key presses to a discobox's terminal
  [36mcapture[39m                   Print a discobox's screen and scrollback
  [36mwait[39m                      Wait until a discobox is blocked, finished, idle, or exits
  [36mevents[39m                    Print discoboxes' state changes as they happen
  [36madopt[39m                     Ask a person to let this discobox lead another
  [36mrelease[39m                   Give a child discobox back

[1mInterface:[0m
  [36mconsole, c[39m                Open the discobox console

[1mFiles & ports:[0m
  [36mcp, scp[39m                   Copy files to and from a discobox
  [36mpush[39m                      Push local commits to a discobox, for it to rebase onto
  [36mproxy[39m                     Forward a discobox's listening ports to local ports
  [36mtools, tool, t[39m            Run a development tool against a discobox

[1mResources:[0m
  [36msecret, secrets[39m           Manage project secrets
  [36mtrust, trusts[39m             Manage the hosts discoboxes trust by a pinned certificate

[1mSetup:[0m
  [36mconfigure, config[39m         Set the default harness and manage what is saved to each
  [36madmin[39m                     Manage advanced Discobox configuration

[1mOther:[0m
  [36mcompletion[39m                Generate shell completion script
  [36mversion[39m                   Print the client and server versions
  [36mhelp[39m                      Help about any command

[1mOptions:[0m
      [36m--color WHEN[39m     set color WHEN to auto, always, or never (default auto)
      [36m--debug[39m          print HTTP requests and the git commands run on this machine
  [36m-h, --help[39m           help for discobox
  [36m-o, --output FORMAT[39m  output FORMAT: table or json (default table)
      [36m--server SERVER[39m  connect to SERVER, an endpoint or a registered server's name; defaults to the primary "discobox admin remote primary" set, and
to the local server when none is
      [36m--token TOKEN[39m    bearer TOKEN for API requests
  [36m-v, --version[39m        print the client and server versions

Use "discobox [command] --help" for more information about a command.
bash-5.2$
